1
00:00:00,330 --> 00:00:02,175
On January seventh, twenty twenty four,

2
00:00:02,195 --> 00:00:04,972
soldiers in Ecuador were getting ready to move one

3
00:00:04,992 --> 00:00:07,770
prisoner. The most powerful gang leader in the country.

4
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:09,635
When they went to get him,

5
00:00:09,655 --> 00:00:10,878
his cell was empty.

6
00:00:12,098 --> 00:00:14,732
Nobody could say exactly when he had left.

7
00:00:14,752 --> 00:00:16,722
Or how. Within forty eight hours,

8
00:00:16,742 --> 00:00:19,376
a TV studio was stormed live on air,

9
00:00:19,396 --> 00:00:22,030
and the president declared war on the gangs.

10
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:24,605
For the next year and a half,

11
00:00:24,625 --> 00:00:26,748
he was the most wanted man in Ecuador.

12
00:00:26,768 --> 00:00:28,355
And when they finally found him,

13
00:00:28,375 --> 00:00:29,426
he was hiding underground.

14
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:31,301
In the city where he was born.

15
00:00:32,841 --> 00:00:35,017
Chapter 1. The boy from Manta.

16
00:00:37,117 --> 00:00:39,739
His name is José Adolfo Macías Villamar.

17
00:00:39,759 --> 00:00:42,759
Everyone in Ecuador knows him by one word.

18
00:00:42,779 --> 00:00:43,137
Fito.

19
00:00:43,857 --> 00:00:47,091
He was born in nineteen seventy nine in Manta,

20
00:00:47,111 --> 00:00:49,622
a port city on Ecuador's Pacific coast.

21
00:00:49,642 --> 00:00:51,429
Manta is known for tuna,

22
00:00:51,449 --> 00:00:52,876
fishing boats and beaches.

23
00:00:52,896 --> 00:00:54,322
In the two thousands,

24
00:00:54,342 --> 00:00:57,214
it also became a gateway for something else.

25
00:00:57,934 --> 00:01:00,087
Ecuador sits between Colombia and Peru,

26
00:01:00,107 --> 00:01:02,622
the two biggest cocaine producers on earth.

27
00:01:02,642 --> 00:01:05,881
Fishing boats and shipping containers from its coast became

28
00:01:05,901 --> 00:01:07,692
a route to Central America,

29
00:01:07,712 --> 00:01:09,502
the United States and Europe.

30
00:01:10,222 --> 00:01:12,110
And the violence grew with it.

31
00:01:12,130 --> 00:01:14,971
In twenty eighteen, Ecuador's murder rate was around six

32
00:01:14,991 --> 00:01:16,243
per hundred thousand people.

33
00:01:16,263 --> 00:01:17,515
By twenty twenty three,

34
00:01:17,535 --> 00:01:19,104
it was more than forty.

35
00:01:19,124 --> 00:01:21,965
One of the fastest rises in violence ever recorded

36
00:01:21,985 --> 00:01:22,919
in the region.

37
00:01:23,639 --> 00:01:25,168
Around two thousand five,

38
00:01:25,188 --> 00:01:27,103
a gang formed in Manabí,

39
00:01:27,123 --> 00:01:28,652
the province around Manta.

40
00:01:28,672 --> 00:01:32,136
It took its name from the town of Chone.

41
00:01:32,156 --> 00:01:32,910
Los Choneros.

42
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:36,442
According to Ecuadorian and international reporting,

43
00:01:36,462 --> 00:01:40,690
Los Choneros started as a local crew and grew

44
00:01:40,710 --> 00:01:43,995
into the country's most powerful criminal group,

45
00:01:44,015 --> 00:01:46,355
moving drugs for foreign cartels,

46
00:01:46,375 --> 00:01:48,243
including, according to U.S.

47
00:01:48,263 --> 00:01:50,131
prosecutors, Mexico's Sinaloa cartel.

48
00:01:50,851 --> 00:01:52,410
Fito was not the founder.

49
00:01:52,430 --> 00:01:53,674
He started lower down.

50
00:01:53,694 --> 00:01:55,569
But by the late twenty tens,

51
00:01:55,589 --> 00:01:58,413
he was widely described as the gang's second in

52
00:01:58,433 --> 00:01:58,728
command.

53
00:01:59,448 --> 00:02:01,797
In twenty eleven, he was arrested.

54
00:02:01,817 --> 00:02:04,956
He was convicted of crimes including organized crime,

55
00:02:04,976 --> 00:02:06,535
drug trafficking and murder,

56
00:02:06,555 --> 00:02:08,114
and sentenced, in total,

57
00:02:08,134 --> 00:02:09,693
to thirty four years.

58
00:02:10,413 --> 00:02:13,022
For most people, that would be the end of

59
00:02:13,042 --> 00:02:14,190
the story. For Fito,

60
00:02:14,210 --> 00:02:16,234
prison was where his real career began.

61
00:02:17,774 --> 00:02:19,845
Chapter 2. The first escape.

62
00:02:21,945 --> 00:02:23,707
In February twenty thirteen,

63
00:02:23,727 --> 00:02:26,381
Fito was held in La Roca,

64
00:02:26,401 --> 00:02:29,499
a small maximum security prison in Guayaquil.

65
00:02:29,519 --> 00:02:30,390
Ecuador's toughest.

66
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:34,005
On February eleventh, he and seventeen other prisoners broke

67
00:02:34,025 --> 00:02:36,920
out. Some of them were members of Los Choneros.

68
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:40,407
The escape was an embarrassment for the government.

69
00:02:40,427 --> 00:02:42,497
Within months, Fito was caught again,

70
00:02:42,517 --> 00:02:44,239
and sent back behind bars.

71
00:02:44,959 --> 00:02:46,949
It was a lesson Fito would remember.

72
00:02:46,969 --> 00:02:49,246
Even Ecuador's toughest prison could not hold him.

73
00:02:49,266 --> 00:02:51,830
And the people guarding him could not always be

74
00:02:51,850 --> 00:02:52,117
trusted.

75
00:02:52,837 --> 00:02:55,838
This time, he would not try to escape for

76
00:02:55,858 --> 00:02:57,180
more than ten years.

77
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:58,858
He did not need to.

78
00:02:58,878 --> 00:03:00,537
Because inside the prison system,

79
00:03:00,557 --> 00:03:03,222
Los Choneros were becoming the people in charge.

80
00:03:04,162 --> 00:03:06,396
Chapter 3. King of the Regional.

81
00:03:08,496 --> 00:03:09,895
In December twenty twenty,

82
00:03:09,915 --> 00:03:11,669
the leader of Los Choneros,

83
00:03:11,689 --> 00:03:13,444
a man known as Rasquiña,

84
00:03:13,464 --> 00:03:15,218
was shot dead in Manta.

85
00:03:15,238 --> 00:03:17,347
The gang needed a new boss.

86
00:03:18,067 --> 00:03:21,103
It was Fito. And he ran Los Choneros from

87
00:03:21,123 --> 00:03:23,819
a cell, in the Regional prison in Guayaquil,

88
00:03:23,839 --> 00:03:26,875
part of the same complex as La Roca and

89
00:03:26,895 --> 00:03:27,894
the Litoral Penitentiary.

90
00:03:28,614 --> 00:03:31,306
From inside, according to prosecutors and journalists,

91
00:03:31,326 --> 00:03:33,632
gang leaders gave orders by phone,

92
00:03:33,652 --> 00:03:35,957
controlled who lived in which wing,

93
00:03:35,977 --> 00:03:38,282
and collected money from other prisoners.

94
00:03:38,302 --> 00:03:41,770
One former inmate told Primicias that prisoners paid Los

95
00:03:41,790 --> 00:03:44,483
Choneros ten to twenty dollars a week.

96
00:03:44,503 --> 00:03:47,196
That claim could not be independently verified.

97
00:03:47,916 --> 00:03:50,012
Rival gangs saw an opening.

98
00:03:50,032 --> 00:03:51,705
Los Lobos, Los Tiguerones,

99
00:03:51,725 --> 00:03:55,514
Los Chone Killers. Many of them had once been

100
00:03:55,534 --> 00:03:57,208
allies of Los Choneros.

101
00:03:57,228 --> 00:03:59,324
Now they wanted its routes.

102
00:04:00,044 --> 00:04:02,565
The war was fought inside the prisons.

103
00:04:02,585 --> 00:04:04,380
In February twenty twenty one,

104
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:07,648
seventy nine prisoners were killed in a single day,

105
00:04:07,668 --> 00:04:09,463
in riots across three prisons.

106
00:04:09,483 --> 00:04:11,641
In September, at the Litoral Penitentiary,

107
00:04:11,661 --> 00:04:14,183
more than one hundred and sixteen died.

108
00:04:14,203 --> 00:04:15,272
Some were beheaded.

109
00:04:15,992 --> 00:04:17,560
In November twenty twenty one,

110
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:20,102
sixty eight more were killed at the Litoral.

111
00:04:20,122 --> 00:04:22,008
By the end of that year,

112
00:04:22,028 --> 00:04:24,867
more than three hundred prisoners had died in Ecuador's

113
00:04:24,887 --> 00:04:27,726
prisons. Most of the dead were members of rival

114
00:04:27,746 --> 00:04:30,268
gangs. The prisons had become the front line.

115
00:04:30,988 --> 00:04:32,793
And in the middle of it,

116
00:04:32,813 --> 00:04:34,010
according to later reporting,

117
00:04:34,030 --> 00:04:35,531
Fito was living very comfortably.

118
00:04:36,251 --> 00:04:39,387
When soldiers finally entered his part of the prison,

119
00:04:39,407 --> 00:04:41,140
they filmed what they found.

120
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:43,244
According to the news site Primicias,

121
00:04:43,264 --> 00:04:44,997
citing CNN, he had lived,

122
00:04:45,017 --> 00:04:46,400
quote, like a king.

123
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:48,504
A large bed. A mini fridge.

124
00:04:48,524 --> 00:04:50,959
Fighting roosters. His own patch of lawn.

125
00:04:51,679 --> 00:04:55,390
A security expert told CNN that Fito had TV,

126
00:04:55,410 --> 00:04:57,464
internet, food, alcohol and women.

127
00:04:57,484 --> 00:04:58,707
Everything he wanted.

128
00:04:59,427 --> 00:05:02,822
InSight Crime, quoting former officials who did not give

129
00:05:02,842 --> 00:05:04,339
their names, went further.

130
00:05:04,359 --> 00:05:06,236
A bar. A sound system.

131
00:05:06,256 --> 00:05:07,754
A pool. Special meals,

132
00:05:07,774 --> 00:05:09,271
approved with medical certificates.

133
00:05:09,291 --> 00:05:12,306
These claims have not been proven in court.

134
00:05:12,326 --> 00:05:14,583
But nobody disputes the main point.

135
00:05:14,603 --> 00:05:17,238
Fito was not living like a prisoner.

136
00:05:17,958 --> 00:05:19,245
He also made videos.

137
00:05:19,265 --> 00:05:21,532
In one, partly filmed inside the prison,

138
00:05:21,552 --> 00:05:24,472
a mariachi band and his own daughter sing a

139
00:05:24,492 --> 00:05:26,105
song about him. In another,

140
00:05:26,125 --> 00:05:27,739
he sits at a table,

141
00:05:27,759 --> 00:05:29,045
surrounded by armed men,

142
00:05:29,065 --> 00:05:30,352
and talks about peace.

143
00:05:31,292 --> 00:05:33,177
Chapter 4. The candidate.

144
00:05:35,277 --> 00:05:36,909
In twenty twenty three,

145
00:05:36,929 --> 00:05:39,386
Ecuador held an early presidential election.

146
00:05:39,406 --> 00:05:42,276
One of the candidates was Fernando Villavicencio,

147
00:05:42,296 --> 00:05:45,992
a former journalist who had built his career investigating

148
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:46,404
corruption.

149
00:05:47,124 --> 00:05:48,983
Villavicencio campaigned against the gangs.

150
00:05:49,003 --> 00:05:52,364
And he said in public that he had been

151
00:05:52,384 --> 00:05:54,619
threatened. By people from Fito's organization.

152
00:05:55,339 --> 00:05:57,463
On August ninth, twenty twenty three,

153
00:05:57,483 --> 00:06:00,321
as he left a campaign event in Quito,

154
00:06:00,341 --> 00:06:01,751
Villavicencio was shot dead.

155
00:06:02,471 --> 00:06:05,519
It was eleven days before the first round of

156
00:06:05,539 --> 00:06:08,247
voting. A suspected gunman died at the scene.

157
00:06:08,267 --> 00:06:09,952
Six Colombian men were arrested.

158
00:06:09,972 --> 00:06:13,020
Two months later, all six were killed inside a

159
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:15,748
prison in Guayaquil, before they could be tried.

160
00:06:16,468 --> 00:06:18,023
Fito's name came up immediately.

161
00:06:18,043 --> 00:06:20,858
He has never been convicted of any role in

162
00:06:20,878 --> 00:06:21,488
the killing.

163
00:06:22,208 --> 00:06:25,631
Three days later, thousands of police and soldiers stormed

164
00:06:25,651 --> 00:06:27,543
the Regional. Photos showed Fito,

165
00:06:27,563 --> 00:06:29,073
stripped to his underwear,

166
00:06:29,093 --> 00:06:32,516
being led out. He was taken to La Roca,

167
00:06:32,536 --> 00:06:34,811
the maximum security prison next door.

168
00:06:35,531 --> 00:06:38,222
For a moment, it looked like the state had

169
00:06:38,242 --> 00:06:40,331
finally taken control. It did not last.

170
00:06:41,051 --> 00:06:42,601
His lawyers went to court.

171
00:06:42,621 --> 00:06:45,427
They argued his life was at risk in La

172
00:06:45,447 --> 00:06:47,311
Roca. A panel of judges agreed.

173
00:06:47,331 --> 00:06:50,137
And within weeks, Fito was back in the Regional.

174
00:06:51,077 --> 00:06:53,206
Chapter 5. The empty cell.

175
00:06:55,306 --> 00:06:57,100
In November twenty twenty three,

176
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:58,551
Daniel Noboa became president.

177
00:06:58,571 --> 00:07:00,002
He was thirty five.

178
00:07:00,022 --> 00:07:02,905
He had promised to take back the prisons.

179
00:07:03,625 --> 00:07:06,577
The son of one of the richest men in

180
00:07:06,597 --> 00:07:08,229
the country, a banana exporter,

181
00:07:08,249 --> 00:07:09,880
Noboa had little political experience.

182
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:11,862
But he had a clear message.

183
00:07:11,882 --> 00:07:13,844
The prisons belonged to the state,

184
00:07:13,864 --> 00:07:14,834
not the gangs.

185
00:07:15,554 --> 00:07:17,656
In early January twenty twenty four,

186
00:07:17,676 --> 00:07:19,777
the government prepared a new operation.

187
00:07:19,797 --> 00:07:22,959
Soldiers would enter the Regional and move Fito to

188
00:07:22,979 --> 00:07:24,373
La Roca. This time,

189
00:07:24,393 --> 00:07:25,081
for good.

190
00:07:25,801 --> 00:07:27,422
On Sunday, January seventh,

191
00:07:27,442 --> 00:07:30,705
the operation began. And Fito was not there.

192
00:07:32,225 --> 00:07:34,562
To this day, Ecuador has not given a full

193
00:07:34,582 --> 00:07:36,396
public account of how he got out.

194
00:07:37,116 --> 00:07:40,212
The official version is that he left hours before

195
00:07:40,232 --> 00:07:43,327
the operation. A government spokesman said the most likely

196
00:07:43,347 --> 00:07:46,443
explanation was that information about the transfer had leaked.

197
00:07:47,163 --> 00:07:49,084
But other officials told different stories.

198
00:07:49,104 --> 00:07:51,995
A former minister said on the radio that Fito

199
00:07:52,015 --> 00:07:53,289
had escaped weeks earlier,

200
00:07:53,309 --> 00:07:56,200
and that a look alike had taken his place.

201
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:58,141
That claim has never been confirmed.

202
00:07:58,861 --> 00:08:01,881
According to CNN, guards in charge admitted the system

203
00:08:01,901 --> 00:08:04,922
was so broken that nobody had even noticed he

204
00:08:04,942 --> 00:08:05,598
was missing.

205
00:08:06,318 --> 00:08:09,881
And the Regional was not even officially a maximum

206
00:08:09,901 --> 00:08:13,463
security prison. Ecuador's most dangerous gang leader had spent

207
00:08:13,483 --> 00:08:17,046
years in what Primicias described as a medium security

208
00:08:17,066 --> 00:08:17,445
facility.

209
00:08:18,165 --> 00:08:21,690
On January eighth, prosecutors charged two prison guards in

210
00:08:21,710 --> 00:08:23,265
connection with the escape.

211
00:08:23,285 --> 00:08:26,810
More than three thousand police and soldiers searched the

212
00:08:26,830 --> 00:08:29,567
complex. Roofs. Sewers. There was no tunnel.

213
00:08:29,587 --> 00:08:31,143
He was simply gone.

214
00:08:32,483 --> 00:08:34,194
Chapter 6. War.

215
00:08:36,294 --> 00:08:38,016
What happened next shocked the world.

216
00:08:38,736 --> 00:08:42,192
On January eighth, Noboa declared a state of emergency.

217
00:08:42,212 --> 00:08:45,668
Within hours, riots broke out in prisons across the

218
00:08:45,688 --> 00:08:47,600
country. Guards were taken hostage.

219
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:50,690
Videos showed some of them threatened at knifepoint.

220
00:08:51,410 --> 00:08:54,041
Another gang leader, from Los Lobos,

221
00:08:54,061 --> 00:08:57,577
also escaped. Bombs went off in several cities.

222
00:08:57,597 --> 00:08:59,345
Police officers were kidnapped.

223
00:09:00,065 --> 00:09:01,627
Then, on January ninth,

224
00:09:01,647 --> 00:09:05,186
armed men in masks burst into the studio of

225
00:09:05,206 --> 00:09:06,768
TC Television in Guayaquil.

226
00:09:06,788 --> 00:09:08,349
During a live broadcast.

227
00:09:08,369 --> 00:09:10,722
Staff were forced to the floor.

228
00:09:10,742 --> 00:09:13,490
Viewers watched it happen in real time,

229
00:09:13,510 --> 00:09:15,467
before police stormed the building.

230
00:09:16,187 --> 00:09:18,386
Thirteen men were arrested at the studio.

231
00:09:18,406 --> 00:09:21,240
Nobody was killed. But the images spread around the

232
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:23,776
world within minutes. For many people outside Ecuador,

233
00:09:23,796 --> 00:09:26,629
it was the first time they had heard of

234
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:27,897
the country's gang war.

235
00:09:28,617 --> 00:09:31,600
That same day, Noboa signed a decree.

236
00:09:31,620 --> 00:09:35,461
Ecuador, he said, was in an internal armed conflict.

237
00:09:35,481 --> 00:09:38,035
Twenty two gangs, including Los Choneros,

238
00:09:38,055 --> 00:09:39,751
were declared terrorist organizations.

239
00:09:39,771 --> 00:09:42,754
The army was ordered to neutralize them.

240
00:09:43,474 --> 00:09:45,144
Soldiers took over the prisons.

241
00:09:45,164 --> 00:09:47,847
Inmates were stripped, shaved and photographed in rows.

242
00:09:47,867 --> 00:09:50,888
The government said it was taking back control of

243
00:09:50,908 --> 00:09:53,929
a prison system that gangs had run for years.

244
00:09:54,649 --> 00:09:55,903
And somewhere in Ecuador,

245
00:09:55,923 --> 00:09:58,769
the man whose escape had started it all was

246
00:09:58,789 --> 00:09:59,087
watching.

247
00:10:00,827 --> 00:10:02,515
Chapter 7. The manhunt.

248
00:10:04,615 --> 00:10:07,735
Fito's family did not wait to find out what

249
00:10:07,755 --> 00:10:10,874
would happen. His wife and children had been living

250
00:10:10,894 --> 00:10:12,967
in Córdoba, Argentina. That same month,

251
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:14,014
Argentina expelled them.

252
00:10:14,734 --> 00:10:18,136
In Ecuador, Fito became the face of the war.

253
00:10:18,156 --> 00:10:19,657
His photo was everywhere.

254
00:10:19,677 --> 00:10:21,559
Police and soldiers raided houses,

255
00:10:21,579 --> 00:10:23,460
farms and hideouts. Each time,

256
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:24,981
he was not there.

257
00:10:25,701 --> 00:10:28,011
Rumors spread that he had left the country.

258
00:10:28,031 --> 00:10:29,468
That he was in Colombia.

259
00:10:29,488 --> 00:10:30,633
Or Mexico. Or dead.

260
00:10:30,653 --> 00:10:33,255
In the end, he had never gone far at

261
00:10:33,275 --> 00:10:33,546
all.

262
00:10:34,266 --> 00:10:37,874
Meanwhile, Ecuador changed a rule it had held for

263
00:10:37,894 --> 00:10:41,501
decades. In a referendum in April twenty twenty four,

264
00:10:41,521 --> 00:10:45,128
voters approved allowing Ecuadorian citizens to be extradited abroad.

265
00:10:45,148 --> 00:10:47,949
Until then, the constitution had banned it.

266
00:10:48,669 --> 00:10:51,366
Months passed. In July twenty twenty four,

267
00:10:51,386 --> 00:10:53,307
Interpol issued a red notice.

268
00:10:53,327 --> 00:10:56,024
Fito was now wanted around the world.

269
00:10:56,744 --> 00:10:59,021
And in April twenty twenty five,

270
00:10:59,041 --> 00:11:01,318
a federal grand jury in Brooklyn,

271
00:11:01,338 --> 00:11:02,850
New York, indicted Fito.

272
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:04,381
Seven counts. Cocaine trafficking.

273
00:11:04,401 --> 00:11:07,827
And smuggling guns from the United States to Ecuador.

274
00:11:08,547 --> 00:11:11,929
U.S. prosecutors say he oversaw cocaine shipments bound for

275
00:11:11,949 --> 00:11:15,331
the United States, and that Los Choneros bought guns

276
00:11:15,351 --> 00:11:17,976
in America and smuggled them into Ecuador.

277
00:11:17,996 --> 00:11:20,244
On the main drug charge alone,

278
00:11:20,264 --> 00:11:22,890
the maximum sentence is life in prison.

279
00:11:23,610 --> 00:11:25,262
According to the indictment,

280
00:11:25,282 --> 00:11:28,188
Los Choneros worked with Mexico's Sinaloa cartel,

281
00:11:28,208 --> 00:11:31,114
and used violence to protect their routes.

282
00:11:31,134 --> 00:11:33,204
Fito has pleaded not guilty.

283
00:11:33,924 --> 00:11:36,868
Noboa was re-elected in April twenty twenty five.

284
00:11:36,888 --> 00:11:38,350
Fito was still missing.

285
00:11:38,370 --> 00:11:41,314
It had now been more than fifteen months.

286
00:11:42,254 --> 00:11:44,128
Chapter 8. Under the floor.

287
00:11:46,228 --> 00:11:47,804
On June twenty fifth,

288
00:11:47,824 --> 00:11:51,394
twenty twenty five, police and soldiers surrounded a house

289
00:11:51,414 --> 00:11:52,990
in Manta. Fito's hometown.

290
00:11:53,710 --> 00:11:55,780
The operation lasted about ten hours.

291
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:58,916
Officials later said not a single shot was fired.

292
00:11:59,636 --> 00:12:01,901
Fito was not hiding in the house.

293
00:12:01,921 --> 00:12:03,207
He was under it.

294
00:12:03,227 --> 00:12:05,493
In an underground hideout beneath the property.

295
00:12:07,013 --> 00:12:08,655
Accounts of the bunker differ.

296
00:12:08,675 --> 00:12:10,981
Some reports described it as surprisingly comfortable.

297
00:12:11,001 --> 00:12:13,972
Others say troops brought in heavy machinery and began

298
00:12:13,992 --> 00:12:16,963
to dig, and that Fito came out when the

299
00:12:16,983 --> 00:12:18,292
digging got too close.

300
00:12:19,012 --> 00:12:21,487
How they found him is also disputed.

301
00:12:21,507 --> 00:12:24,694
One report says intelligence officers noticed the strange behavior

302
00:12:24,714 --> 00:12:26,119
of a local official.

303
00:12:26,139 --> 00:12:29,326
Another says the final confirmation came from his young

304
00:12:29,346 --> 00:12:32,533
daughter. The government has not given one official answer.

305
00:12:33,253 --> 00:12:35,156
What is clear is the result.

306
00:12:35,176 --> 00:12:38,040
Five hundred and thirty five days after his cell

307
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:40,283
was found empty, Fito was in custody.

308
00:12:40,303 --> 00:12:43,167
Four men described as his bodyguards were arrested with

309
00:12:43,187 --> 00:12:46,050
him. They were later sentenced to four years in

310
00:12:46,070 --> 00:12:47,332
prison for hiding him.

311
00:12:48,052 --> 00:12:49,707
Noboa announced the capture himself.

312
00:12:49,727 --> 00:12:51,382
He thanked the security forces,

313
00:12:51,402 --> 00:12:54,396
and credited two new laws on intelligence and security.

314
00:12:54,416 --> 00:12:57,411
And he said Ecuador was ready to send Fito

315
00:12:57,431 --> 00:12:58,751
to the United States.

316
00:12:59,471 --> 00:13:01,053
For a year and a half,

317
00:13:01,073 --> 00:13:03,456
the most wanted man in Ecuador had been hiding

318
00:13:03,476 --> 00:13:04,524
in his own hometown.

319
00:13:06,064 --> 00:13:07,578
Chapter 9. Brooklyn.

320
00:13:09,678 --> 00:13:11,400
Fito was flown to Guayaquil,

321
00:13:11,420 --> 00:13:13,142
and locked in La Roca.

322
00:13:13,162 --> 00:13:15,580
The prison he had escaped from once,

323
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:16,974
and avoided for years.

324
00:13:17,694 --> 00:13:19,143
In July twenty twenty five,

325
00:13:19,163 --> 00:13:20,907
at a court hearing in Ecuador,

326
00:13:20,927 --> 00:13:22,376
he agreed to be extradited.

327
00:13:23,096 --> 00:13:25,493
On July twentieth, he was put on a plane

328
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:27,910
to New York. He was the first Ecuadorian to

329
00:13:27,930 --> 00:13:29,521
be extradited by his own country.

330
00:13:30,241 --> 00:13:32,947
The next day, he stood in federal court in

331
00:13:32,967 --> 00:13:35,673
Brooklyn. The same court that had tried El Chapo.

332
00:13:35,693 --> 00:13:37,793
He pleaded not guilty to all charges.

333
00:13:38,513 --> 00:13:40,802
The comparison was hard to miss.

334
00:13:40,822 --> 00:13:44,265
Joaquín El Chapo Guzmán also escaped from prison twice,

335
00:13:44,285 --> 00:13:47,344
in Mexico. He was extradited in twenty seventeen,

336
00:13:47,364 --> 00:13:49,653
tried in that same Brooklyn courthouse,

337
00:13:49,673 --> 00:13:51,192
and sentenced to life.

338
00:13:51,212 --> 00:13:54,655
Today he is held in the federal supermax prison

339
00:13:54,675 --> 00:13:55,425
in Colorado.

340
00:13:56,145 --> 00:13:59,360
He is held in the Metropolitan Detention Center in

341
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:01,158
Brooklyn. Not a private wing.

342
00:14:01,178 --> 00:14:03,315
Not a lawn. Not fighting roosters.

343
00:14:04,035 --> 00:14:06,491
Since then, his case has moved slowly.

344
00:14:06,511 --> 00:14:08,966
Hearings have been postponed again and again.

345
00:14:08,986 --> 00:14:10,734
As of our latest check,

346
00:14:10,754 --> 00:14:12,149
no trial had begun,

347
00:14:12,169 --> 00:14:14,978
and no plea deal had been made public.

348
00:14:15,698 --> 00:14:18,679
According to Primicias, his lawyer has also raised concerns

349
00:14:18,699 --> 00:14:21,680
about his health and his medical care in custody.

350
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:24,681
For now, the man who once had his own

351
00:14:24,701 --> 00:14:27,682
lawn in prison spends his days in a federal

352
00:14:27,702 --> 00:14:28,682
jail cell, waiting.

353
00:14:30,022 --> 00:14:31,885
Chapter 10. After Fito.

354
00:14:33,985 --> 00:14:35,915
So did catching Fito end the war?

355
00:14:36,635 --> 00:14:39,318
Not really. Los Choneros did not disappear.

356
00:14:39,338 --> 00:14:42,022
Other gangs kept fighting for their routes.

357
00:14:42,042 --> 00:14:45,498
Ecuador's murder rate stayed among the highest in Latin

358
00:14:45,518 --> 00:14:45,884
America.

359
00:14:46,604 --> 00:14:49,756
In fact, twenty twenty five became the most violent

360
00:14:49,776 --> 00:14:51,519
year in Ecuador's recorded history,

361
00:14:51,539 --> 00:14:53,634
with more murders than ever before.

362
00:14:53,654 --> 00:14:56,454
Removing one leader did not remove the business.

363
00:14:57,174 --> 00:14:58,711
Prison massacres continued too.

364
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:00,657
In November twenty twenty five,

365
00:15:00,677 --> 00:15:04,160
Ecuador moved hundreds of its most dangerous prisoners into

366
00:15:04,180 --> 00:15:06,106
a new maximum security prison,

367
00:15:06,126 --> 00:15:09,219
El Encuentro. It opened before it was finished.

368
00:15:09,939 --> 00:15:11,278
But Fito's story changed something.

369
00:15:11,298 --> 00:15:13,725
A gang leader who once ran his own wing

370
00:15:13,745 --> 00:15:16,171
of a prison, with a lawn and a bar,

371
00:15:16,191 --> 00:15:18,618
is now an inmate in a federal jail in

372
00:15:18,638 --> 00:15:20,521
New York, waiting for an American court.

373
00:15:21,241 --> 00:15:23,787
And one question still has no official answer.

374
00:15:23,807 --> 00:15:26,675
How did Ecuador's most powerful prisoner walk out of

375
00:15:26,695 --> 00:15:28,279
a prison full of guards,

376
00:15:28,299 --> 00:15:29,883
and why did nobody notice?

377
00:15:30,603 --> 00:15:32,791
What do you think happened that night?

378
00:15:32,811 --> 00:15:34,367
Tell us in the comments.

379
00:15:34,387 --> 00:15:37,206
And to see where Ecuador sent its most dangerous

380
00:15:37,226 --> 00:15:39,729
prisoners next, watch our story about El Encuentro,

381
00:15:39,749 --> 00:15:40,675
on this channel.
